'#Language "WWB-COM"

'Option Explicit

' Library to convert infix math expression to postfix math expressions, which can be evaluated more systematically
' Also includes a function to create VBA code to evaluate postfix expressions for Result1DComplex objects
'
' IMPORTANT: Output objects of math functions need to be compatible with input object: 1) same min, 2) same max), 3) same number of samples
' It should be assumed that input objects represent true functions: x values increase strictly monotonically
' The result should also always be stored in the input object "Operand"
'
' Copyright 2010-2023 Dassault Systemes Deutschland GmbH
' -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' History of Changes:
' -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' 29-Aug-2024 fsr: Added new component product & division functions for 3D fields; applied character based truncation to functions and operators as well.
' 29-Aug-2024 fsr: Clarified "Division by 3D fields not supported" error message, which would also get triggered when dividing by a product of multiple factors
' 02-Mar-2023 mha: Changed rule for adding linebreaks in ShowSupportedOperators as regarding constants to a system based on number of characters instead of number of constants
' 02-Mar-2023 mha: Changed constant PlanckH to 6.62607015e-34 in accordance with the 2019 redefinition of SI base units
' 02-Mar-2023 mha: Changed constant names to be consistent with global constants to be used in expressions / parameter (former names still work, but are not shown in msgbox) 
' 22-Apr-2020 fsr: Added a rudimentary format check for InfixToPostfix
' 28-Oct-2019 fsr: Load parameter values by RunID if possible
' 12-Sep-2018 ebu,fsr: Set the imaginary part to zero for XYZMag(), MagnitudeByComponent3D
' 03-May-2018 fsr: Accept numbers in scientific format using capital E to denote exponent
' 18-Oct-2017 fsr: Added Log and Log10 for 3D fields
' 28-Jun-2017 fsr: Fixed Sum & CumSum
' 27-Feb-2017 fsr: Switched from legacy Mue0 to Mu0 (Mue0 still works for bwc); added option to create 3D constant scalar field (constant numerical value
'					will be expanded to 3D const field automatically); fixed a problem with tiny imaginary parts in ComplexScalarMult3D
' 27-Sep-2016 fsr: Added "Sum" and "CumSum" operations
' 06-Sep-2016 fsr: Fixed problem with negative sign in 2nd (or higher) arguments, e.g. "Atn2(A,-B)"
' 01-Sep-2016 fsr: Added Modulo, Remainder, Round, Floor, Ceiling functions
' 20-May-2016 fsr: Fixed definition of QElectron
' 09-May-2016 fsr: Fixed Boolean functions for non-complex inputs
' 02-May-2016 fsr: Added "Boolean" functions GTR, GEQ, LSS, LEQ, EQL, EQLtol, NEQ, NOT
' 08-Feb-2016 fsr: Added option to create constant 3d vector field, 3D trigonometric functions
' 19-Nov-2015 fsr: Nicefied 'ShowSupportedOperators'
' 09-Nov-2015 fsr: Implemented Sqr3D for 1DC; added Planck's constant
' 17-Mar-2015 fsr: Finalized 3D framework; fixed arity detection for nested functions
' 16-Dec-2014 fsr: Implemented complex ScalarMult, ScalarCompMult
' 15-Dec-2014 fsr: Fixed Log101DC, MagdB201DC; Added a number of 3D functions
' 09-Dec-2014 fsr: Extended framework for 3D results (Real/Imag functions etc)
' 05-Dec-2014 fsr: Fixed Im1DC
' 03-Dec-2014 fsr: Overall performance improvements; added derivative and integral functions
' 11-Jul-2014 fsr: IsNumeric check is now always carried out using US locale
' 25-Apr-2014 mku: Added Sinh, Asinh, Cosh, Acosh
' 21-Nov-2013 fsr: Added framework for mix 3D results
' 25-Jul-2012 fsr: Added Heaviside/unit step function
' 04-Apr-2012 fsr: Fixed a bug in the Min/Max/Mean1D functions
' 14-Mar-2012 fsr: New functions: PhD, ArcD, MagdB10, MagdB20, UPh, UArc, UPhD, UArcD
' 29-Jan-2012 fsr: Added a check if numerical expressions are followed by a proper operator
' 20-Oct-2011 fsr: fixed a problem with commas as separator in number formating;
'					array indexes now use "long" so that plots With more than 32k samples can be handled
' 08-Sep-2011 fsr: added function Sgn(z)
' 15-Jul-2011 fsr: moved the actual implementation of ztan, zatn, and zatn2 into complex.lib, improved parameter handling for functions with arity>1
' 01-Jun-2011 fsr: "Stack(UBound(Stack))=-0" caused problems in Linux, changed to "Stack(UBound(Stack))=CStr(0)"
' 26-Apr-2011 fsr: fixed a problem where constants like "Pi" would not work for non-US locales
' 22-Apr-2011 fsr: new function "Abscissa" allows to extract the "x" value of a template, useful for example if "Frequency" is needed in a formula
' 06-Apr-2011 fsr: finished framework for functions with arity>1, separator for parameters is sParaSep; included functions Atn2 and Atn2d
' 22-Feb-2011 fsr: included some physical and mathematical constants, fixed some bugs related to the CosD, ACosD, ATn, ATnD functions
' 17-Feb-2011 fsr: included "Xe-Y" expressions. Xe(Y) and Xe(-Y) are not working, but VBA does not recognize these as numeric, either
' 07-Feb-2011 fsr: remapped ^ operator from NthPower to new ZthPower
' 25-Oct-2010 fsr: adjusted for DS - changed all "Report*ToWindow" calls to "Report*" calls
' 13-Oct-2010 fsr: minor changes
' 11-Oct-2010 fsr: added min/max/mean/Ln/Log10 functions, straightened up a little
' 04-Oct-2010 fsr: included ".XX" for "0.XX" and "XeY" expressions, arbitrary capitalization for functions, improved parameter recognition&handling
' 22-Sep-2010 fsr: initial version
' -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

' The include below is only necessary when "Main" is active for testing:
''include "complex.lib"

Public Const sParaSep_LIB = "," ' Use this character to separate parameters for functions with arity >1

' Currently supported operators, sorted by priority, plus corresponding command and number of arguments (arity), separated by |
